  "title": "Scott-continuous posit category",
  "description": "The scott-continuous posit category generated by positing inside the transfinite predication category. Positing packages the transfinite predication-fiber-functor as a predication-fibration in this generated term. Its objects are scott-continuous posit traces over a fixed base (L, C, E), and its hom-classes are sub-singletons presented by the pointwise-and-stepwise knowledge-order relation on predication valuations. The base parameters, predication-fibration, and object traces present the category; bounds and homs are reconstructed from the trace family and active knowledge-order comparison witnesses.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "lattice",
    "predicate-category",
    "entity-set",
    "predication-fibration",
    "traces"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
